{title: It Carries A Great Reward}
{subtitle: Hebrews 10:35–36}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Remember the days when light broke through
[Gm]You endured the hard struggle and pain [Bb/D]
[Eb]Publicly exposed to the world's view
Side by side [Gm]with the ones in [F]chains
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Gm]Suffered with the prisoners in the [F]dark
[Gm]Accepted the loss of what was [Eb]yours [F]
[Gm]Joyfully took the seizure of your [F]mark
Knowing [Eb]your treasure is far more secure
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So do not [Bb]throw away your [F/A]confidence now
It [Gm]carries a great reward [Eb]for your soul
[Bb]You need endurance to hold [F/A]your ground
Un[Gm]til you receive what God [Eb]foretold
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]You had a better and lasting possession [F/A]
[Gm]Not things that decay or fade away [Gm7/D]
[Eb]But a hope that stands in its session
While the world [Gm]turns and shifts its [F]day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Gm]Do not let your spirit shrink [F]back
[Bb]My soul takes no pleasure in [Eb]fear [F]
[Gm]The one who is coming will not [F]lack
And [Eb]will not delay in coming here
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So do not [Bb]throw away your con[F/A]fidence now
It [Gm]carries a great reward [Eb]for your soul
[Bb]You need endurance to hold [F/A]your ground
Un[Gm]til you receive what God [Eb]foretold
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm]My righteous one will live by [F]faith
Not a[Bb]mong those who [F/A]shrink and are de[Gm]stroyed
But [Cm]preserving the soul in this [F]age
With [Eb]the promise of life as our joy
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Hold fast to the [F/A]faith
It will not be lost in the [Gm]dark
Hold fast to the [Eb]faith
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] |
